ge Scripps College Facts FAQs Contact Us Academic Experience Faculty Majors & Minors Academic Resources Accommodations and Academic Resource Services Clark Humanities Museum Department of Natural Sciences European Union Center Humanities Institute Intercollegiate Feminist Center Library Registrar Scripps College Press Williamson Gallery Post-Bacc Program Research Study Abroad Life & Community New Students Creating Community Leadership Center Residential Vibrancy Student Services Contact Us CARE@SCRIPPS Career Planning & Resources Tiernan Field House Title IX Close Search Scripps College Search Scripps College > Student Services > Career Planning & Resources Career Planning & Resources Home Contact Us CARE@SCRIPPS Career Planning & Resources Tiernan Field House Title IX Career Planning & Resources (CP&R) equips Scripps students and alumnae to recognize and build on their strengths, connect their liberal arts education and experiences to meaningful possibilities, and pursue lives of purpose with confidence, courage, and hope. Our signature programming includes: The Career Action Plan , a self-paced, flexible career development program available to all students through Canvas Career Exploration Treks, a cohort-based program visiting organizations and employers in major cities Resume Refresh, connecting Scripps students with alums in their industry for both resume feedback and a networking opportunity Summer Internship Grants, providing funding for students pursuing low-paid or unpaid Summer internships For Current Students: Did you know that CP&R has an entire website full of resources on Inside Scripps ? Access that here using your Scripps single sign-on account. You can learn more about our signature programs, our counseling services (both general and industry-specific), and our employer recruitment events. Need to schedule an appointment with our career team? Use Handshake to schedule, also using your Scripps single sign-on. You can also c heck out Handshake for industry guides , career advice , and our job board (including on – campus jobs). Want to connect with the Scripps Community? Alums and families are on Olive Grove —which allows you unlimited free messages to the Scripps community (a perk compared to the paid tiers on LinkedIn). Download our Career Services Guide for templates, guides and best practices for everything career-focused, or stop by CP&R for your own printed copy . Get to know us on our Inside Scripps Meet the Team page, or stop by CP&R any time! We are located in Seal Court right next door to the Motley, and our office is open every weekday from 9 A.M. to 5 P.M. Information for... Scripps Alums Employers and Recruiters Scripps Families Internships Contact Us Post-Grad The Scripps Advantage 4/5 first years meet with CP&R 2/3 pursue postgrad education 5 years complete advanced degree Value of a Scripps Degree Earning potential: Scripps alums outperform the national average in terms of the earnings gap between college and high school graduates Higher graduate income : Six years after graduation, Scripps alums’ median income is 44 percent higher than the national average Fewer federal student loans : Scripps students are 28 percent less reliant on federal student loans than the national average Less debt : Average debt at graduation is roughly $8,000 lower than the national average Greater return on investment: Scripps students can expect a greater return on their education compared to similar students nationally *Data sources: US Department of Education, Integrate Postsecondary Education Data System, and WASC Senior College and University Commission Support Scripps Students Learn more about how you can support Scripps students through paid internships, job opportunities, sponsoring career treks, volunteering, and more! Contact CP&R for more information (909) 621-8180 or [email protected] . Latest News About Scripps Visit Campus Apply Now 1030 Columbia Avenue Claremont, CA 91711 (909) 621-8000 Campus Map Virtual Tour Diversity Centennial Celebration Strategic Plan Employment Scripps Forward: Centennial Campaign Scripps Merchandise Emergency Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Higher Education Emergency Relief Fund (HEERF) Campus Hazing Transparency Report The Claremont Colleges . © Scripps College | Accessibility | Nondiscrimination Statement | Privacy"
