    "https://www.scrippscollege.edu/hr/faculty/tenure-track-position-in-computational-organic-chemistry-in-the-department-of-natural-sciences-pitzer-and-scripps-college": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Position in Computational Organic Chemistry in the Department of Natural Sciences Pitzer and Scripps College",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Position in Computational Organic Chemistry in the Department of Natural Sciences Pitzer and Scripps College | Scripps College in Claremont, California Close About Scripps At a Glance Assessment and Institutional Research Annual Financial Reports WASC Reaffirmation Process History College Timeline History of the Presidency Scripps College Traditions Initiatives Centennial (Strategic) Plan Diversity Sustainability Centennial Celebration Our Campus Scripps Merchandise Administration President Board of Trustees Senior Leadership Claremont Colleges Admission & Aid Apply First-Year Applicants Transfer Applicants QuestBridge Applicants International Applicants Homeschool Applicants Veteran Applicants Dates and Deadlines Financial Aid Visit Why Scripps College Scripps College Facts FAQs Contact Us Academic Experience Faculty Majors & Minors Academic Resources Accommodations and Academic Resource Services Clark Humanities Museum Department of Natural Sciences European Union Center Humanities Institute Intercollegiate Feminist Center Library Registrar Scripps College Press Williamson Gallery Post-Bacc Program Research Study Abroad Life & Community New Students Creating Community Leadership Center Residential Vibrancy Student Services Contact Us CARE@SCRIPPS Career Planning & Resources Tiernan Field House Title IX Inside Scripps Alums Families Careers Giving Events Directory Inside Scripps Alums Families Careers | Giving Events Directory \"> About Scripps At a Glance Assessment and Institutional Research Annual Financial Reports WASC Reaffirmation Process History College Timeline History of the Presidency Scripps College Traditions Initiatives Centennial (Strategic) Plan Diversity Sustainability Centennial Celebration Our Campus Scripps Merchandise Administration President Board of Trustees Senior Leadership Claremont Colleges Admission & Aid Apply First-Year Applicants Transfer Applicants QuestBridge Applicants International Applicants Homeschool Applicants Veteran Applicants Dates and Deadlines Financial Aid Visit Why Scripps College Scripps College Facts FAQs Contact Us Academic Experience Faculty Majors & Minors Academic Resources Accommodations and Academic Resource Services Clark Humanities Museum Department of Natural Sciences European Union Center Humanities Institute Intercollegiate Feminist Center Library Registrar Scripps College Press Williamson Gallery Post-Bacc Program Research Study Abroad Life & Community New Students Creating Community Leadership Center Residential Vibrancy Student Services Contact Us CARE@SCRIPPS Career Planning & Resources Tiernan Field House Title IX Close Search Scripps College Search Working at Scripps College Faculty Positions Tenure-Track Position in Computational Organic Chemistry in the Department of Natural Sciences Pitzer and Scripps College August 24, 2026 Tenure-Track Position in Computational Organic Chemistry in the Department of Natural Sciences Pitzer and Scripps College Faculty Positions The Department of Natural Sciences seeks to hire a tenure-track teacher-scholar to teach in our organic chemistry program and to lead a student-centered undergraduate research program in computational chemistry. There are also opportunities to design and teach both upper-level electives and courses for non-science majors. We seek a chemist with a clear capacity for and dedication to excellence in teaching, who will develop a vibrant research program that fully engages undergraduate students, and who possesses a demonstrated commitment to our colleges’ (Pitzer and Scripps) goal of improving higher education student learning. The appointment will be at the Assistant Professor level and will begin on July 1, 2027. A Ph.D. in a chemistry-related field and a record of scholarly publication are required. Postdoctoral experience is strongly preferred. The Department, which houses the biology, chemistry, physics, neuroscience, and environmental science faculty for Pitzer and Scripps Colleges (two of the five undergraduate Claremont Colleges), offers innovative and interdisciplinary programs in the natural sciences. The Department supports faculty success through mentorship, professional development opportunities, and regular sabbaticals. Faculty of the Department of Natural Sciences are part of the rich intellectual environment of the Claremont Colleges consortium and benefit from close proximity to major research universities in the Southern California region, enabling collaboration both within and outside the department. Additional information about the department may be found at https://natsci.claremont.edu/ . The salary for this position will range from $105,000 – $111,000 and will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. Current faculty benefits include a generous tuition-remission program for children of faculty, which can potentially cover up to half their tuition at most colleges in the U.S., and a 12% employer contribution to a 403b retirement plan. Applications should be uploaded to: apply.interfolio.com/192187 and must include (1) a cover letter describing your interest in and capacity for the position, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a concise statement of plans for an independent research program that will involve undergraduates, not exceeding 6 pages, (4) a 1-2-page statement describing your approach to teaching and how you make learning accessible to all students, regardless of preparation, life experience, and scientific background, and (5) the upload of 3 recommendation letters. Inquiries regarding the position may be e-mailed to Professor Anna Wenzel at [email protected] . Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026 , and the position will remain open until filled. The Department of Natural Sciences of Pitzer and Scripps Colleges is an equal-opportunity employer. In keeping with its ongoing commitment to build and support a diverse and equitable academic community, the Department of Natural Sciences actively encourages applications from women and members of historically underrepresented groups. Tags About Scripps Visit Campus Apply Now 1030 Columbia Avenue Claremont, CA 91711 (909) 621-8000 Campus Map Virtual Tour Diversity Centennial Celebration Strategic Plan Employment Scripps Forward: Centennial Campaign Scripps Merchandise Emergency Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Higher Education Emergency Relief Fund (HEERF) Campus Hazing Transparency Report The Claremont Colleges . © Scripps College | Accessibility | Nondiscrimination Statement | Privacy"
    },
